          "title": "DONE — commit 7ff3b59 (single commit with T014 focus work, branch feat/action-task-c, PR #244). Diagnosis: no regression existed — most control surfaces never passed a rest glow, so glow_size had nothing to scale at rest. Fix (user-directed model): theme owns the glow COLOR (theme.glow + per-widget tones), the config glow_size setting owns the AMOUNT (none/thin/medium/large via the scaled_glow chokepoint), and the new interaction.control_rest_glow token + base-level PaintCx::rest_glow(radius) give every surface a faint rest halo: Button P/D/Outline (tight REST_GLOW_RADIUS=12 at rest; hover halo unchanged), Input, Toggle track, Checkbox box, Select trigger, Pane, DockFrame fill, filled Row cards, styled ScrollRegion, Tag, Alert, Toast (severity-toned). User verified across two GPU rounds; round-3 findings (button halo too wide, toasts/cards/styled-region flat) fixed in the same commit. Deliberately flat: Secondary/Ghost/Link buttons, unfilled rows, RailCell bare-icon rest, frameless ScrollRegion, layout shells, disabled controls. FOLLOW-UP recorded: SDF glyph/text glow renderer capability so Icons can halo (glyphs are text runs; glow is a rect-renderer feature). Docs: widgets.md \"The glow model — who owns what\" + per-widget notes.",
