    {
      "id": "126d0855-658d-471f-86a6-27eb144fc591",
      "phaseId": "99d19246-1ba9-4720-9895-e70c66acf144",
      "number": 299,
      "shortId": "CY8C2",
      "priority": 12,
      "shortName": "scrollregion-keyboard-scroll-a",
      "title": "Keyboard scrolling acts on whatever has focus — one branch, plus the four horizontal actions",
      "status": "canceled",
      "description": "# Keyboard scrolling for any scroll area\n\n# ✅ SHIPPED — the widget half (`096f06e`), unchanged by anything below\n\nEight `WidgetIntent` variants: `ScrollPageUp` / `ScrollPageDown` / `ScrollToTop` / `ScrollToBottom`\nand the four horizontal ones. `ScrollRegion` acts on them:\n\n- it owns the arithmetic — a page is 0.9 of its viewport, the edges clamp — because it is the only\n  thing that knows its viewport and its content;\n- it **declines** an axis it cannot scroll (axis off, or content fits), so a nested region or the host\n  gets a turn; consuming would make the key silently do nothing;\n- handled after the children, so the innermost scrollable region wins, as with the wheel;\n- `keyboard_target(Signal<bool>)` gates which instance responds — per instance, position-agnostic,\n  unset means yes. Bound to the mount's chrome focus by F003/P011/T020\n  (`StateView::container_keyboard_target`).\n\n**The logic lives in the widget, once.** Every `ScrollRegion` anywhere behaves identically with no\nper-usage code. The host only ever says \"one page down, this axis\".\n\n# ⚠️ THE ROUTE CHANGED — 2026-07-29, by the user. This supersedes the 2026-07-16/27 keys.\n\n**Superseded:** vertical `prefix+Home/End/PageUp/PageDown`, horizontal `prefix+Shift+` the same four.\nThat shape existed because there was no other way to stop the keys reaching the terminal.\n\n**Now:** *focus is the mode* (P085(F007) — \"Components declare their actions; chrome focus is the\nmode\"). While a component holds chrome focus nothing is forwarded to a backend, so **plain\n`PageUp` / `PageDown` / `Home` / `End` are free** and are the container's scroll keys; the existing\n`Shift+` variants stay exactly as they are for the focused *pane*'s scrollback.\n\n**And it is not a new action family.** The bindings already exist and are already global/direct:\n`scroll_page_up = \"Shift+PageUp\"`, `scroll_page_down`, `scroll_to_top = \"Shift+Home\"`,\n`scroll_to_bottom = \"Shift+End\"`, `scroll_line_up/down` (`keybindings.default.toml`), handled today\nagainst the focused terminal viewport. So the app half is:\n\n1. **One branch at the top of those existing handlers**: chrome focus set ⇒ dispatch the matching\n   `Event::Widget(WidgetIntent::Scroll*)` into the chrome tree — the FocusScope (P085/T351) delivers it\n   to the focused container and every other container is inert — else the terminal viewport path,\n   unchanged. One binding, one meaning: *scroll whatever has focus*.\n2. **The four horizontal actions** still need adding (`ScrollPageLeft/Right`, `ScrollToLeftEdge/RightEdge`\n   — the widget intents exist, no `WmAction` does), through the full Adding-New-Actions checklist\n   (AGENTS.md): variant → `action_from_name` → `action_priority` → `action_policy()` → handler →\n   `build_registry` → `keybindings.default.toml` → `ActionRegistry::ALL` descriptor **with its `args`\n   declaration** → `rpc.rs` → README. Reuse `ResizeAxis` (`heca/src/input.rs:40`) if an axis argument is\n   preferred over four names — optional, defaulting to vertical, so a plain binding stays legal\n   (a *required* argument would forbid a bare key, F003/P010/T006).\n3. A **declined** intent stops at the chrome; it does **not** fall through to the pane. The\n   innermost-wins rule is about nested *scroll areas*, and the pane is not an outer scroll area of the\n   sidebar.\n\n**This half is specified in P085(F007)/T352 step 5** (the routing task) — whichever is picked up first,\ndo not implement it twice. What remains uniquely here is the horizontal action family.\n\n# Still ruled out (2026-07-28, checked in code — do not re-open)\n\nFeeding these through the **widget keymap** (`build_widget_keymap`, `heca/src/app/registry.rs:202`,\nthe `[keys.widgets]` table). It is consulted at `heca/src/app/events.rs:156` inside a branch that\nrequires **a modal to be open**, so `[keys.widgets]` reaches focused widgets inside modals only.\n\n# The 2026-07-17 blocker is discharged\n\n\"No chrome surface mounts a `ScrollRegion`\" is false since 2026-07-26: containers nest their own\n(`heca/src/providers/workspaces.rs`). `GridKey` still has no `PageUp`/`PageDown` — and does not need\nit, because the intent is semantic. That is the point of not delivering a key.\n\n# Acceptance\n\n- With a container focused, plain `PageUp/PageDown/Home/End` scroll **it**; with a pane focused, the\n  `Shift+` variants scroll the pane's scrollback, as today.\n- Every other scroll area declines; nothing reaches the terminal while a container is focused.\n- Horizontal scrolling reachable from RPC through the same actions, one code path.\n- No second mechanism for the same job.\n- Whole workspace green, clippy 0 warnings.\n- **USER verifies in the app**, with more than one scroll area on screen (P085(F007)/T359 seats the\n  second one).",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [
        {
          "id": "126d0855-658d-471f-86a6-27eb144fc591-check-001-planned-blocked",
          "date": "2026-07-16T23:14:27.765Z",
          "fromStatus": "planned",
          "toStatus": "blocked",
          "title": "Investigated the integration surface this session; recording the routing decision and a hard blocker (no chrome ScrollRegion target) so the next session does not land dead keybindings.",
          "description": "Investigated the integration surface this session; recording the routing decision and a hard blocker (no chrome ScrollRegion target) so the next session does not land dead keybindings."
        },
        {
          "id": "126d0855-658d-471f-86a6-27eb144fc591-check-002-blocked-planned",
          "date": "2026-07-27T20:53:27.489Z",
          "fromStatus": "blocked",
          "toStatus": "planned",
          "title": "Re-checked in code 2026-07-27: the hard blocker is DISCHARGED. The 2026-07-17 claim \"NO chrome surface mounts a grid-ui ScrollRegion — it appears in heca/src ONLY in chrome/realize.rs\" is now false. `build_sidebar_shell` (heca/src/chrome/mod.rs:1541) mounts a real `ScrollRegion`, restores its offset from `SharedChromeState.workspaces.scroll` through `scroll_to`, and re-stores it from an `on_scroll` listener that ignores host-driven restores (`event: None`). It is called TWICE from `build_chrome_root` (:3129 left, :3150 right), so there are two live app-side targets, not none. F004/P001/T006's first half landed under the 2026-07-26 sidebar work, and its second half (\"SidebarNav cursor calls ensure_visible\") is satisfied by a better mechanism: `Component::wants_visible` (heca-grid-ui/src/component.rs:516), which every scroll area honours, so the keyboard cursor is followed by the library rather than by per-list host wiring. Two of the other 2026-07-17 findings still hold and are now T012's own work, not blockers: there is still no keyboard→chrome-widget-tree routing (nothing in heca/src dispatches `Event::Widget` into the chrome tree), and `GridKey` still has no `PageUp`/`PageDown` — which only matters if the scroll intent reaches the widget as a key, and the task prefers a semantic intent or an imperative call. What is left before building is the routing DECISION (focused-surface, this task's own answer, versus F004/P001/T007's explicit pick-mode); that is the user's call, not mine.",
          "description": "Re-checked in code 2026-07-27: the hard blocker is DISCHARGED. The 2026-07-17 claim \"NO chrome surface mounts a grid-ui ScrollRegion — it appears in heca/src ONLY in chrome/realize.rs\" is now false. `build_sidebar_shell` (heca/src/chrome/mod.rs:1541) mounts a real `ScrollRegion`, restores its offset from `SharedChromeState.workspaces.scroll` through `scroll_to`, and re-stores it from an `on_scroll` listener that ignores host-driven restores (`event: None`). It is called TWICE from `build_chrome_root` (:3129 left, :3150 right), so there are two live app-side targets, not none. F004/P001/T006's first half landed under the 2026-07-26 sidebar work, and its second half (\"SidebarNav cursor calls ensure_visible\") is satisfied by a better mechanism: `Component::wants_visible` (heca-grid-ui/src/component.rs:516), which every scroll area honours, so the keyboard cursor is followed by the library rather than by per-list host wiring. Two of the other 2026-07-17 findings still hold and are now T012's own work, not blockers: there is still no keyboard→chrome-widget-tree routing (nothing in heca/src dispatches `Event::Widget` into the chrome tree), and `GridKey` still has no `PageUp`/`PageDown` — which only matters if the scroll intent reaches the widget as a key, and the task prefers a semantic intent or an imperative call. What is left before building is the routing DECISION (focused-surface, this task's own answer, versus F004/P001/T007's explicit pick-mode); that is the user's call, not mine."
        },
        {
          "id": "126d0855-658d-471f-86a6-27eb144fc591-check-003-in-progress-blocked",
          "date": "2026-07-27T23:42:19.401Z",
          "fromStatus": "in-progress",
          "toStatus": "blocked",
          "title": "Half shipped, half blocked (2026-07-28). The WIDGET half is done and committed in `096f06e`: eight `WidgetIntent::Scroll*` variants (page and edge, both axes), `ScrollRegion` acting on them — it owns the paging arithmetic and the clamp because it is the only thing that knows its viewport and content — declining any axis it cannot scroll so a nested region or the host gets a turn, handled after the children so the innermost wins like the wheel, plus `ScrollRegion::keyboard_target(Signal<bool>)` which gates which instance responds and is per-instance and position-agnostic. Tests included, and the gating was verified by flipping the signal. The APP half cannot be built honestly yet: it must target the container that holds keyboard focus, and there is no such thing until F003/P011/T020 (`FocusDock`) lands. Everything else about it is settled and written in the description — the four actions through the full Adding-New-Actions checklist, the bindings (`prefix+Home/End/PageUp/PageDown`, Shift for horizontal), the dispatch into the chrome tree where every non-focused container declines. No keybindings exist yet, so there are no dead keys in the meantime.",
          "description": "Half shipped, half blocked (2026-07-28). The WIDGET half is done and committed in `096f06e`: eight `WidgetIntent::Scroll*` variants (page and edge, both axes), `ScrollRegion` acting on them — it owns the paging arithmetic and the clamp because it is the only thing that knows its viewport and content — declining any axis it cannot scroll so a nested region or the host gets a turn, handled after the children so the innermost wins like the wheel, plus `ScrollRegion::keyboard_target(Signal<bool>)` which gates which instance responds and is per-instance and position-agnostic. Tests included, and the gating was verified by flipping the signal. The APP half cannot be built honestly yet: it must target the container that holds keyboard focus, and there is no such thing until F003/P011/T020 (`FocusDock`) lands. Everything else about it is settled and written in the description — the four actions through the full Adding-New-Actions checklist, the bindings (`prefix+Home/End/PageUp/PageDown`, Shift for horizontal), the dispatch into the chrome tree where every non-focused container declines. No keybindings exist yet, so there are no dead keys in the meantime."
        },
        {
          "id": "126d0855-658d-471f-86a6-27eb144fc591-check-004-blocked-planned",
          "date": "2026-07-28T12:27:03.803Z",
          "fromStatus": "blocked",
          "toStatus": "planned",
          "title": "Its one blocker is discharged: F003/P011/T020 landed chrome focus (a container id + per-mount keyboard_target signals), so \"which area obeys\" now has an answer. The route it had settled is superseded by the user's 2026-07-29 decision (focus is the mode), which shrinks this task to one branch in the existing scroll handlers plus the four horizontal actions — recorded in the description.",
          "description": "Its one blocker is discharged: F003/P011/T020 landed chrome focus (a container id + per-mount keyboard_target signals), so \"which area obeys\" now has an answer. The route it had settled is superseded by the user's 2026-07-29 decision (focus is the mode), which shrinks this task to one branch in the existing scroll handlers plus the four horizontal actions — recorded in the description."
        },
        {
          "id": "126d0855-658d-471f-86a6-27eb144fc591-check-005-planned-canceled",
          "date": "2026-07-28T12:32:57.291Z",
          "fromStatus": "planned",
          "toStatus": "canceled",
          "title": "Unified into P085(F007)/T352 (VKF85, \"Focus is the mode\") at the user's request 2026-07-30 — the two said the same thing once the route changed to focus-is-the-mode. Every section this task still carried was transferred into T352 verbatim first: the shipped widget half (096f06e), the superseded prefix-gated keys, the four horizontal actions still to add, the widget-keymap route ruled out (events.rs:156 is modal-only), and the discharged 2026-07-17 blocker. Canceled rather than done — the work is not done, it has one home now.",
          "description": "Unified into P085(F007)/T352 (VKF85, \"Focus is the mode\") at the user's request 2026-07-30 — the two said the same thing once the route changed to focus-is-the-mode. Every section this task still carried was transferred into T352 verbatim first: the shipped widget half (096f06e), the superseded prefix-gated keys, the four horizontal actions still to add, the widget-keymap route ruled out (events.rs:156 is modal-only), and the discharged 2026-07-17 blocker. Canceled rather than done — the work is not done, it has one home now."
        }
      ],
